{
  "title": "SingleEntryLayout",
  "description": "CacheLayout for a representation that occupies one record. This is what almost every asset type wants: the codec produced one value, and the cache keeps that one value. It is the default an AssetType carries, so a type that needs nothing else declares nothing at all. Raise the version when the codec's stored representation changes shape. Records written under the old version stop being found and are re-acquired.",
  "symbol": "SingleEntryLayout",
